WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:15.095
My name is Elizabeth Willard, and I am a 22-year-old teacher.

2
00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:21.980
I graduated from the Hartford Female Seminary in Connecticut, one of the first schools in America that trains

3
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.182
female teachers.

4
00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:30.467
In 1854 I began teaching in the new territory of Kansas, an area located in the middle of

5
00:00:30.527 --> 00:00:31.488
the United States.

6
00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:37.618
There are many teaching jobs in the West because many whites have been settling here from the East.

7
00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:41.060
New frontier towns have popped up everywhere.

8
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.982
My teacher training started when I was twenty, and I learned spelling, mathematics, and music.

9
00:00:49.263 --> 00:00:54.766
Before graduation my classmates and I were invited to teach out West when we completed our studies.

10
00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:59.728
Some teaching students accepted the offer, and I was one of them.

11
00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:05.606
We trained for frontier life by carrying pails of water and chopping firewood.

12
00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:09.748
We needed to be tough to face the many hardships ahead.

13
00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:16.712
When we graduated, a school committee gave us our teaching posts, and I was assigned to a school

14
00:01:16.772 --> 00:01:17.472
in Kansas.

15
00:01:18.693 --> 00:01:23.935
All the teachers traveled west in the spring, and since it was unsafe for women to travel alone,

16
00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:25.496
my father went with me.

17
00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:33.933
First, we rode on horseback for two weeks, about eight hundred kilometers, from Hartford, Connecticut, to Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

18
00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:41.638
Then, we took a steamboat down the Ohio River from Pittsburgh through the states of Ohio and Kentucky.

19
00:01:42.879 --> 00:01:49.283
After 12 days we arrived in Old Shawneetown, Illinois, and from there I took a stagecoach on my

20
00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:57.792
own. After ten days and another eight hundred kilometers, I arrived at my final destination—Fort Leavenworth, Kansas.

21
00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:04.554
Suddenly I was alone in a strange town, and I had nowhere to stay.

22
00:02:05.635 --> 00:02:07.075
So I went to the schoolhouse.

23
00:02:08.396 --> 00:02:13.097
With so few trees for lumber on the prairie, sod and dirt had been used to build the

24
00:02:13.137 --> 00:02:15.018
small school, rather than wood.

25
00:02:15.758 --> 00:02:17.898
There was only one room and two windows.

26
00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:22.760
The bathroom was outside, and a little fence wrapped around the schoolyard.

27
00:02:24.172 --> 00:02:26.513
Some of the town's children came by to see me.

28
00:02:27.554 --> 00:02:31.136
One little girl named Abby said I would be staying with her family.

29
00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:36.939
"Boarding around," or staying in students' homes, is common for frontier teachers.

30
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.763
I would have to help Abby's family with the chores, but I was happy to accept their offer.

31
00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:50.347
Boarding helps me save money, since I make only one hundred and fifty dollars a year—half the salary

32
00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:51.268
of a male teacher.

33
00:02:52.352 --> 00:02:57.375
Most of my students live on farms, so the school year must fit between the fall harvest and

34
00:02:57.415 --> 00:02:58.436
the spring planting.

35
00:02:59.556 --> 00:03:04.259
During my first year, the class size varied from 3 to 25 children.

36
00:03:05.259 --> 00:03:09.962
Some of the children do farm work and other chores and cannot attend every day.

37
00:03:11.043 --> 00:03:14.144
My students' ages range from four to twenty years old.

38
00:03:15.105 --> 00:03:20.248
In my classroom I have a small desk up front, and my students sit on benches in rows.

39
00:03:21.196 --> 00:03:24.899
There is one blackboard, and we have no books except for a Bible.

40
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.763
Sometimes the children bring in old newspapers or magazines from home.

41
00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:35.968
We have no paper supplies, so my students write their lessons on flat rocks called slates.

42
00:03:37.229 --> 00:03:39.972
They write with a soft piece of rock called a slate pen.

43
00:03:42.474 --> 00:03:46.777
Most of my students behave well in class, but sometimes I have to punish them.

44
00:03:48.158 --> 00:03:52.481
If a child talks during a lesson, I put a whispering stick in his or her mouth.

45
00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:58.382
This is a small wooden stick that is held in place by a piece of cloth that I

46
00:03:58.442 --> 00:03:59.863
tie around the student's head.

47
00:04:00.803 --> 00:04:04.044
The child is forced to bite on the stick and cannot speak.

48
00:04:05.804 --> 00:04:11.226
Sometimes if a student never knows the correct answer to a question, I put a pointy hat on

49
00:04:11.266 --> 00:04:13.646
their head with the word "Dunce" written on it.

50
00:04:14.827 --> 00:04:19.408
When a student wears the dunce cap, it means he or she is not very smart.

51
00:04:20.496 --> 00:04:22.457
My first winter was very hard.

52
00:04:23.257 --> 00:04:26.899
The temperature sometimes dropped to -23 degrees Celsius.

53
00:04:27.899 --> 00:04:31.821
The snow started falling in November and did not stop until April.

54
00:04:33.041 --> 00:04:38.203
The only heat we had was a potbellied stove in the classroom, and it was smoky and hard

55
00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:38.683
to light.

56
00:04:39.464 --> 00:04:42.745
I'd arrive at school early to chop firewood for the whole day.

57
00:04:43.766 --> 00:04:46.247
Children close to the stove would get too hot.

58
00:04:47.227 --> 00:04:49.508
Others, in the back of the room, almost froze.

59
00:04:50.472 --> 00:04:55.934
It was so cold that my students' lunches of dried fruit and salted meat would sometimes freeze.

60
00:04:57.135 --> 00:05:00.156
Some children became sick and died during the year.

61
00:05:02.217 --> 00:05:04.998
We all were happy when spring finally arrived.

62
00:05:07.259 --> 00:05:10.821
I am now at the end of my first year, and I am very lonely.

63
00:05:11.841 --> 00:05:17.103
When I took this job, I promised not to marry for two years, so I could devote myself

64
00:05:17.143 --> 00:05:17.964
to my students.

65
00:05:18.932 --> 00:05:22.036
In my free time, I sew quilts and patch my clothes.

66
00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:25.800
I go to church and visit the friends I have met there.

67
00:05:27.442 --> 00:05:32.347
I have heard that some teachers have already gone home because the life out here is too difficult.

68
00:05:33.288 --> 00:05:35.451
But I would like to stay on for another year.

69
00:05:36.512 --> 00:05:39.916
I have grown to love my students and the progress we all have made.
